file construction/ITINERARY.md the round's entry, and both %481 accounts folded whole
obs THE RENUMBER SWEPT A PEER'S LABEL, AND readme_reach CAUGHT IT. A peer published %492 while I worked, so my row renumbered to %500 by the derived spine -- the stamp is the key and did not move. I did that with a blanket s/%492/%500/g across my own files, and the operator card was one of them: it carried a peer's own pointer, [%492](archive/REDS-two-algorithms-agreeing-rows-492.md), and my sweep changed the LABEL while leaving the path. A renumber is a sweep over MY citations, and a card holds everyone's. Reverted; the guard that found it reads links rather than numbers, which is why it could see what a number-aware sweep could not.
obs AND IT UNCOVERED AN UPSTREAM BREAK BESIDE MINE. The same readme_reach red named a second card link, to REDS-the-verdict-travelled-and-the-reason-did-not-rows-492.md, where the file on disk is rows-494.md. My diff shows I never touched that line, so it arrived with the rebase. Repaired in passing -- one character pair, and the guard reds every tree in the fleet until someone does it. reds_fold reds only because it asks readme_reach to run, so the two were one fault.
obs THE DAY SHELF WENT MISORDERED WITHOUT ANYONE WRITING A WRONG ROW. My row was prepended under the delimiter, then the rebase merged four peers' newer-stamped rows in ABOVE it, and index_row_bound reads newest-first as a law. Sorted the shelf's rows by stamp rather than hand-placing mine, so the fix holds for the next rebase too.
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md the walk-back cairn, and the condensation I withdrew
scope one keystone -- the four Mantra field-count guards taught to count; the Aurora three named
obs THE HOT PASS COST ME A LAP THE WAY %483 SAYS IT WILL. Two reds arrived from my own round -- reds_ledger_headline and reds_ledger_monotone both read the ledger's headline SPAN, which my hand-edited Rows line left at 491 while the spine measured 492. The guard names its own repair, reds_ledger_headline_write.sh write, and both are green after it. The lesson is the tree's own: a number a hand types beside a number a program measures is a number that will disagree, and the writer exists because it already had.
status GREEN for this round -- four limbs green, the new rung green at 0s, limb1 proven red on a real fourth field, and the ledger headline repaired by its own writer. The hot pass closes guard_red on two rows that are not this round's: sow_allow_reach, which reds on any tree with no seed/ projection (an environment fact, and projecting is another lane's), and standing_equipment, which is %483 reading the previous pass's card -- the lap that closes a red still closing guard_red, exactly as that row predicts.
recommend check in (Keaton) -- the identity gap is unblocked by measurement rather than by a word: widening Line now reds limb1 honestly, so the placard moves with the code and the seam is a decision you can make rather than a wall.
